      <h2 class="section-title mb-12">Where MEAICON makes the difference in retail</h2>
      <div class="reveal grid-2">
        <div class="prose-content">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Omnichannel inventory synchronisation</h3>
          <p>Modern regional retailers operate across physical stores, mobile apps and online marketplaces — and customers expect real-time stock visibility across all channels. MEAICON delivers the secure connectivity links between stores, warehouses and e-commerce platforms that enable click-and-collect, ship-from-store and real-time inventory sync. Low-latency WAN connections ensure that stock levels update within seconds, not hours, preventing oversold items and lost sales.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">PCI-DSS payment security infrastructure</h3>
          <p>Every card transaction touches networks that must meet PCI-DSS requirements. MEAICON designs and deploys segmented payment networks with encryption, tokenisation support and continuous monitoring — isolating cardholder data environments from retail operations traffic. Our approach reduces audit scope, accelerates PCI compliance and protects against the growing wave of payment-targeting attacks across the our region.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal grid-2 mt-8">
        <div class="prose-content">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Customer analytics at the edge</h3>
          <p>Forward-looking retailers are deploying edge compute in stores to process footfall analytics, heat mapping and customer journey data in real time — without sending raw video to the cloud. MEAICON provides the edge infrastructure and secure connectivity that makes in-store analytics possible, enabling personalised promotions, queue management and layout optimisation while keeping customer data within regulatory boundaries.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">regional retail at a glance</h3>
          <p>The regional retail market is projected to exceed $500 billion by 2027, with e-commerce growing at 15–20% annually across the GCC and Africa. Saudi Arabia and the UAE lead digital commerce adoption, with mobile commerce accounting for over 60% of online transactions. Payment fraud attempts in the region rose 35% year-on-year, making PCI-aligned infrastructure non-negotiable. Meanwhile, the African retail sector is rapidly formalising, with intra-regional trade and mobile money platforms creating new omnichannel opportunities.</p>
